  ],
  "description": "Two of the four-device ternary inverters in series, with the second stage driven from the first stage output through its own 10 kOhm gate resistor. The second gate bus is a real load on the first output: its gate capacitance and the summing resistance of stage one are in that path, so each stage slows the one before it. The definition is two inverter tables in series, so pin y should follow pin a and lag it by both stages."
}